            "project": {
              "content": "# Static support boundaries\n\nThis project isolates Vercel AI SDK preparation callbacks, uses one function tool to call another agent, and retains a workflow agent outside the selected ToolLoopAgent target.\n",
              "digest": "sha256:a2a415c0242c7b41f52f8313a2f7c31cca3bde3e9673204c7fc2bc1a2efce29f",
              "path": "/moldea/project.md",
              "scalarLength": 206,
              "utf8ByteLength": 206
            },
            "runtimes": [
              {
                "asset": {
                  "content": "# Vercel AI SDK preparation boundaries\n\nThe project uses static inspection conservatively around preparation callbacks:\n\n- `supportAgent` uses `prepareCall`, so only its `ToolLoopAgent` definition and `callOptionsSchema` relationship are statically proved. Its effective instruction, output schema, and tools may be replaced for each call.\n- `stepSupportAgent` uses `prepareStep`, so its agent definition, input schema, output schema, and `get_status` tool relationships remain statically proved, while its effective instruction may be replaced for each step.\n- `delegatingSupportAgent` registers `delegate_support` as an ordinary function tool. The tool implementation calls `stepSupportAgent`, but that call does not establish a handoff, routing target, or subagent relationship.\n- `workflowSupportAgent` is a `WorkflowAgent` and remains outside this project's selected `ToolLoopAgent` inspection target.\n",
                  "digest": "sha256:6694f62edb6fde3bbd65c66398d6804bd6be140790cdbdca639c757ac44c6f4a",
                  "path": "/moldea/runtimes/vercel-ai-sdk.md",
                  "scalarLength": 907,
                  "utf8ByteLength": 907
                }
              }
            ],
            "unresolved": {}
          },
